---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="Set up HomeADE" description="How to install HomeADE on a Mac or Windows PC, make a vault, sign in your agents, and open the first window.">
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 2rem)">
    <div class="wrap guide">
      <h1>Set up HomeADE</h1>
      <p>HomeADE is the project desk for the agents on this computer. It runs Claude, Codex, or Grok beside your notes. Setup on a Mac takes about ten minutes. HomeADE does not need Obsidian or any other app.</p>
      <p><a href="/homeade">About HomeADE</a></p>

      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A Mac with macOS 14 or later. A Windows PC can run the beta, <a href="#windows">below</a>.</li>
        <li>An account with one agent: a Claude plan or Anthropic API key for Claude Code, or an account for Codex or Grok. HomeADE never holds your logins; each tool signs in on its own.</li>
        <li>Nothing else. HomeADE can make your notes folder for you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="mac">1. Install HomeADE on your Mac</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Downloads are by request for now. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=HomeADE%20download`}>{site.email}</a> for the link, open the file, and drag HomeADE to Applications.</li>
        <li>Open HomeADE. Apple has signed and notarized it, so the Mac opens it without a warning. An antenna icon appears in the menu bar. To start HomeADE each time you log in, click the icon and turn on <strong>Open at login</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>A new user sees a <strong>Get started</strong> card on the Today screen. It has four rows: <strong>Machine</strong>, <strong>Vault</strong>, <strong>Agents</strong>, and <strong>Connectors</strong>. Each row has one button that opens the screen for that job. The card counts your progress, for example "1 of 4," until all four are done or you click <strong>Hide</strong>. <strong>Settings → Get started</strong> brings it back.</p>

      <h2 id="machine">2. Machine</h2>
      <p>The machine is the computer that runs HomeADE. For now, that is this Mac. To add your iPhone later, follow <a href="/fieldade/setup">FieldADE setup</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="setup">3. Vault</h2>
      <p>A vault is a folder of notes. If you have none, click <strong>Create a vault</strong>, or open <strong>Settings → Vault → New vault…</strong></p>
      <ol>
        <li>HomeADE asks where to put the vault. It asks each time.</li>
        <li>Type a name, or keep the default, "My Vault."</li>
      </ol>
      <p>HomeADE fills the vault with these folders: 0 Ingest, 1 Projects, 2 Areas, 3 Resources, 4 Archive, 5 Zettelkasten, Journal, Outbox, System, and Templates. It adds a Welcome note, a "Getting started" project with three to-dos, and a "Home" area. The vault is plain Markdown, so Obsidian is not needed, and it can open the vault later. To use a folder you already have, click <strong>Choose a folder</strong>.</p>

      <h2 id="agents">4. Agents</h2>
      <p>HomeADE chats with the official Claude Code, Codex, and Grok command-line tools on this computer. Open <strong>Settings → Agents on this machine</strong>. Each tool shows as installed or not, and signed in or not. At least one must be signed in before chats work.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Install</strong> beside a tool that is missing. Install needs Node.js. On a Mac, install Node from nodejs.org or with Homebrew first, then click <strong>Check again</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Sign in</strong>. HomeADE opens a terminal that is already running that tool's own login. Finish the login there.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Check again</strong>. The tool should now show as signed in.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="connectors">5. Connectors</h2>
      <p>Connectors are optional. Click <strong>Skip for now</strong> to leave them for later. To add one, open <strong>Setup → Connectors</strong>. Rows for Mail, Calendars, and Tickets show a state and, when something fails, a one-line fix. Click <strong>+ Add</strong> to choose Gmail, Cloudflare, Google Calendar, or iCloud, or Jira, Yahoo, Fastmail, AOL, any other IMAP mail, and more.</p>
      <p>Mail uses an app password, not your main one. For Gmail, make it at myaccount.google.com/apppasswords. For iCloud, go to account.apple.com, then <strong>Sign-In and Security → App-Specific Passwords</strong>. Calendar sign-in happens in the <a href="/fieldade/setup">iPhone app</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="windows">Windows (beta)</h2>
      <p>The Windows beta, also by request, runs the same screens in a window and a tray icon. We have not yet tested it on a clean PC, so expect rough edges. It is not yet code-signed, so Windows warns you: click <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. Then follow steps 2 to 5 above. When you click <strong>Install</strong> on an agent, HomeADE installs Node.js first, through winget.</p>

      <h2 id="trouble">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The HomeADE window says it has no token.</strong> Setup is unfinished. Click the antenna icon, then <strong>Set up this Mac…</strong></li>
        <li><strong>An agent says it is not signed in.</strong> Open <strong>Settings → Agents on this machine</strong> and click <strong>Sign in</strong>. Finish the login in the terminal, then click <strong>Check again</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>You have no vault yet.</strong> Click <strong>Create a vault</strong> on the Get started card.</li>
        <li><strong>Chats do not start.</strong> Check that one agent is signed in, then click <strong>Restart HomeADE…</strong> in the menu.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Still stuck? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide { max-width: 44rem; }
  .guide h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; scroll-margin-top: 6.5rem; }
  .guide ol, .guide ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .guide li { margin: .35rem 0; }
  .guide .fine { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted, inherit); margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .cmd { display: flex; align-items: stretch; margin: .5rem 0 1rem; background: var(--band, #16181d); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
  .cmd pre { flex: 1; min-width: 0; margin: 0; padding: .7rem .9rem; color: #f3f1ec; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .copy-btn { flex: none; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .75rem; padding: 0 .8rem; border: 0; border-left: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.2); background: rgba(255,255,255,.08); color: #f3f1ec; cursor: pointer; }
  .copy-btn:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,.18); }
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const text = document.getElementById(btn.dataset.copy).textContent;
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text); btn.textContent = 'Copied'; }
      catch { btn.textContent = 'Press ⌘C'; getSelection().selectAllChildren(document.getElementById(btn.dataset.copy)); }
      setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = 'Copy'), 1500);
    });
  });
</script>
